    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson's Foundation exercise page lists biking, running, Tai Chi, yoga, Pilates, dance, weight training, non-contact boxing and qi gong among exercise types that all have positive effects on PD symptoms; the APTA guideline says results across community-based exercise modes appear comparable for impairment and participation-based measures, suggesting no 1 mode is superior to another, while other comparisons favor 1 intervention over another and the essential components that distinguish more from less effective programs are not clear; a network meta-analysis of mind-body exercises (Bai et al.) concludes that superiority over other exercise modalities remains uncertain. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/treatment/exercise",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:39c69fbaf994e1165c356d81162ab1c4f08b6678efca24be7e6aba4130ac1f9e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
