    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In the Duncan and Earhart randomized trial, 62 participants were assigned to a twice-weekly community-based Argentine tango program or a no-intervention control group and assessed off anti-Parkinson medication; on the primary MDS-UPDRS-3 outcome the control group showed no significant change over 12 months whereas the tango group had a reduction of 28.7% (12.8 points), and the authors suggest that long-term participation in tango may modify progression of disability in PD. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21959675/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a02e1c4f69ef9e82c1823046610a5ff0ef376bc783e9a84db943b687693f2658",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
