        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A meta-analysis of tai chi and qigong trials (Song et al.; 15 RCTs, 755 subjects) reported improvement in UPDRS III (ES=-0.444) and balance (ES=0.544), rated methodological bias low in 6 studies, moderate in 7 and high in 2, and noted that funnel plots suggested some degree of publication bias; a later meta-analysis of traditional Chinese exercises (thirteen RCTs, 859 patients) reported UPDRS-III MD -4.30 and Berg Balance Scale MD 2.63 versus usual control and noted that only one included study used a double-blind procedure. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5618798/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a92106d30d6c4523892a1b9bdcac3c0d8636e2c449ceae9b2565b6e478a672f7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
